7. Additional permission: client deployments by service providers

   This section grants permissions in addition to Section 1. It never
   restricts them. Notwithstanding Section 2, if you are a service provider
   (for example an agency, consultant, freelancer or systems integrator),
   you may install, host, operate, configure, customize and maintain the
   Licensed Work on behalf of a client, and charge that client for those
   services (including hosting, setup, development, maintenance and
   support), provided that all of the following conditions are met:

   (a) Each deployment serves one client (an individual, or an
       organization including its affiliates under common control) for
       that client's own business purposes. The client's employees,
       contractors, customers and end users may use the workflows,
       automations, interfaces and applications the client operates on
       that deployment.

   (b) The deployment is not offered, marketed or made available to
       parties other than that client as a workflow-automation, AI-agent
       or application-building platform, whether multi-tenant,
       self-service or white-labelled.

   (c) Neither you nor the client sells, rents or otherwise provides
       access to the Licensed Work itself as a product (for example
       accounts, seats, workspaces or tenants of the Licensed Work) to
       parties other than that client.

   (d) You give the client a copy of this License, and the client's use
       of the deployment remains subject to it.

   (e) You provide that client, under an agreement with that client,
       services of your own beyond making the Licensed Work available,
       such as setup, configuration, building workflows, interfaces or
       integrations, training, maintenance or support. A deployment you
       keep running for up to 90 days after those services end, to hand
       it over to the client, still meets this condition.

   This Section 7 does not cover hosting offerings. A "hosting offering"
   is an offer made to customers generally, under any name or brand,
   whose main purpose is to provide deployments of the Licensed Work that
   you, or a platform or partner acting with you, run for the customer,
   wherever those deployments run: for example one-click or marketplace
   deployments run by the platform, hosting plans or tiers that anyone can
   order, or deployments provisioned through self-service sign-up. Deployments
   sold by advertising the hosting of the Licensed Work as a product of
   its own (for example "LiveContext hosting" or "managed LiveContext")
   are part of a hosting offering. A hosting offering made on a paid
   basis is a competitive offering under Section 2 and requires a
   commercial license.

   Publishing templates, images, scripts or catalogue entries that let
   others deploy the Licensed Work on infrastructure they control and
   operate themselves is not a hosting offering. Describing publicly,
   with prices, the services you provide clients under this Section,
   hosting and maintenance included, is not by itself a hosting
   offering.

   A service provider that operates separate deployments for several
   clients, each meeting the conditions above and none of them part of a
   hosting offering, is not providing a competitive offering under
   Section 2 by doing so. Notwithstanding Section 5, a failure to meet
   these conditions for one deployment terminates the permissions of this
   Section 7 for that deployment only. If you stop a deployment or an
   offering that does not meet this Section 7, or bring it in line, before
   the Licensor notifies you or within 30 days of the Licensor's notice,
   Section 5 does not apply to it, and a deployment brought in line keeps
   the permissions of this Section 7. This applies to the first such
   notice only.

   Building workflows, interfaces, templates or other content with the
   Licensed Work, for yourself or for clients, is always permitted, and
   that content is not part of the Licensed Work, except for any portion
   of the Licensed Work it contains or copies.
